With CSS, you can center images with several methods.

An image can be centered horizontally, vertically, or both.

To display a horizontally centered image, we can usemargin: auto;ordisplay: flex;.

One way to center an image horizontally on a page is to usemargin: auto.

Since the <img> element is an inline element by default (andmargin: autodoes not have any effect on inline elements) we must 
convert the image to a block element, withdisplay: block.

In addition, we have to define awidth. The 
width of the image must be smaller than the width of the page.

